{"title":"Career Roadmap · Assistive Product Designer","role":"Assistive Product Designer","summary":"An Assistive Product Designer designs products and systems that help people with disabilities, injuries, age-related limitations, or temporary functional challenges perform everyday activities more independently, safely, comfortably, and confidently.","facts":{"Current degree":"B.Des (Bachelor of Design)","Course":"Healthcare / Medical Product Design"},"about":[],"intro":[],"horizons":[],"sections":[{"heading":"Overview","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An Assistive Product Designer designs products and systems that help people with disabilities, injuries, age-related limitations, or temporary functional challenges perform everyday activities more independently, safely, comfortably, and confidently."},{"type":"p","text":"The field combines industrial design, ergonomics, accessibility, human factors, healthcare, rehabilitation, materials, engineering, and user research."},{"type":"h","text":"Examples include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Mobility aids"},{"text":"Adaptive utensils"},{"text":"Wheelchairs and accessories"},{"text":"Prosthetic interfaces"},{"text":"Orthotic products"},{"text":"Communication aids"},{"text":"Accessible household products"},{"text":"Senior-care products"},{"text":"Adaptive sports equipment"},{"text":"Rehabilitation devices"},{"text":"Assistive technology interfaces"}]},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des Healthcare/Medical Product Design","Assistive Design Intern","Junior Assistive Product Designer","Assistive Product Designer","Senior Designer / Human-Centred Design Specialist","Design Lead / Assistive Technology Innovation Lead"],"label":"Typical route"}]},{"heading":"Career Horizons","kind":"horizons","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Assistive Product Designers can work across:"},{"type":"table","header":["Sector","Opportunities"],"rows":[[{"text":"Rehabilitation"},{"text":"Mobility and rehabilitation products"}],[{"text":"Medical Devices"},{"text":"Patient-support products"}],[{"text":"Disability Technology"},{"text":"Assistive technologies"}],[{"text":"Senior Care"},{"text":"Age-friendly products"}],[{"text":"Prosthetics & Orthotics"},{"text":"User-centred product development"}],[{"text":"Hospitals"},{"text":"Healthcare product innovation"}],[{"text":"Home Healthcare"},{"text":"Adaptive home products"}],[{"text":"Education"},{"text":"Assistive learning products"}],[{"text":"Sports"},{"text":"Adaptive sports equipment"}],[{"text":"Consumer Products"},{"text":"Accessible everyday products"}],[{"text":"NGOs"},{"text":"Community-based assistive solutions"}],[{"text":"Startups"},{"text":"Assistive technology innovation"}],[{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Human factors and accessibility research"}]]}]},{"heading":"Year-by-Year Roadmap","kind":"build","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1 — Human-Centred Design Foundations"},{"type":"p","text":"Build strong foundations in design and human needs."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Design fundamentals"},{"text":"Sketching"},{"text":"Form development"},{"text":"Colour and visual communication"},{"text":"Observation"},{"text":"User research"},{"text":"Basic ergonomics"},{"text":"Anthropometry"},{"text":"Materials"},{"text":"Prototyping"},{"text":"Inclusive design fundamentals"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human body dimensions"},{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Grip strength"},{"text":"Dexterity"},{"text":"Balance"},{"text":"Posture"},{"text":"Mobility"},{"text":"Sensory limitations"},{"text":"Cognitive accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Projects"},{"type":"h","text":"Design simple products such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"One-handed kitchen tool"},{"text":"Easy-grip bottle"},{"text":"Accessible door handle"},{"text":"Adaptive writing tool"},{"text":"Senior-friendly household product"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2 — Accessibility & Assistive Design"},{"type":"p","text":"Move into specialised human-centred design."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Universal design"},{"text":"Inclusive design"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Anthropometry"},{"text":"User interviews"},{"text":"Contextual observation"},{"text":"Co-design"},{"text":"Rapid prototyping"},{"text":"Usability testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Understand different user groups"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"People with mobility limitations"},{"text":"People with visual impairments"},{"text":"People with hearing impairments"},{"text":"People with limited dexterity"},{"text":"Older adults"},{"text":"People recovering from injury"},{"text":"Children requiring adaptive products"},{"text":"People with temporary functional limitations"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Tools"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fusion 360"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"SolidWorks fundamentals"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3 — Professional Assistive Product Development"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop the ability to take a product from research to manufacturable prototype."},{"type":"h","text":"Learn"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical/assistive product requirements"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Safety considerations"},{"text":"Material selection"},{"text":"Mechanical principles"},{"text":"Product architecture"},{"text":"Manufacturing"},{"text":"Rapid prototyping"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Injection moulding fundamentals"},{"text":"Product testing"},{"text":"Usability evaluation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced research"},{"type":"h","text":"Study:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User journey mapping"},{"text":"Task analysis"},{"text":"Functional requirements"},{"text":"Failure modes"},{"text":"Risk identification"},{"text":"Accessibility evaluation"},{"text":"User acceptance"},{"text":"Long-term usability"}]},{"type":"h","text":"The designer should learn to ask:"},{"type":"p","text":"What does the user need to accomplish, and what prevents them from doing it independently?"},{"type":"p","text":"rather than simply designing a visually attractive product."},{"type":"h","text":"Year 4 — Specialisation & Industry Preparation"},{"type":"p","text":"Choose a specific assistive-design direction."},{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Mobility"},{"type":"h","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Wheelchair accessories"},{"text":"Walking aids"},{"text":"Transfer aids"},{"text":"Mobility supports"},{"text":"Seating systems"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Daily Living"},{"type":"h","text":"Design:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Adaptive kitchen products"},{"text":"Dressing aids"},{"text":"Bathroom products"},{"text":"Household tools"},{"text":"Personal-care products"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Sensory Accessibility"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on products for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual accessibility"},{"text":"Hearing accessibility"},{"text":"Tactile interaction"},{"text":"Multi-sensory communication"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Rehabilitation"},{"type":"h","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rehabilitation equipment"},{"text":"Exercise aids"},{"text":"Recovery products"},{"text":"Therapy-support devices"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Assistive Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Combine physical products with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Sensors"},{"text":"Mobile applications"},{"text":"AI"},{"text":"Computer vision"},{"text":"Voice interfaces"},{"text":"Smart-home technology"}]}]},{"heading":"Specialisation Options","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Specialisation","Core Focus"],"rows":[[{"text":"Mobility Products"},{"text":"Movement and independence"}],[{"text":"Adaptive Daily-Living Products"},{"text":"Everyday activities"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation Products"},{"text":"Recovery and therapy"}],[{"text":"Senior-Care Products"},{"text":"Age-friendly design"}],[{"text":"Prosthetic Interfaces"},{"text":"Human-device interaction"}],[{"text":"Orthotic Products"},{"text":"Support and comfort"}],[{"text":"Accessible Technology"},{"text":"Digital + physical accessibility"}],[{"text":"Adaptive Sports"},{"text":"Inclusive performance"}],[{"text":"Children's Assistive Products"},{"text":"Child-centred accessibility"}],[{"text":"Community Assistive Design"},{"text":"Affordable local solutions"}]]}]},{"heading":"Internship Roadmap","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Year 1"},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Accessibility organisations"},{"text":"Design research studios"},{"text":"Social-impact design projects"},{"text":"Community organisations"},{"text":"Product design studios"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 2"},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Rehabilitation centres"},{"text":"Assistive technology companies"},{"text":"Healthcare startups"},{"text":"Medical product companies"},{"text":"Inclusive-design consultancies"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Year 3–4"},{"type":"h","text":"Target:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Medical-device companies"},{"text":"Rehabilitation technology companies"},{"text":"Assistive technology startups"},{"text":"Healthcare innovation labs"},{"text":"Research institutions"},{"text":"Hospital innovation teams"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful internship titles"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assistive Design Intern"},{"text":"Healthcare Design Intern"},{"text":"Medical Product Design Intern"},{"text":"Industrial Design Intern"},{"text":"Human Factors Intern"},{"text":"UX Research Intern"},{"text":"Accessibility Design Intern"},{"text":"Product Development Intern"}]}]},{"heading":"Strong Internship Project","kind":"internships","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"\"Adaptive Kitchen System for People With Limited Hand Dexterity\""},{"type":"h","text":"Step 1 — User Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Understand:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Grip limitations"},{"text":"Range of motion"},{"text":"Common kitchen tasks"},{"text":"Safety concerns"},{"text":"Caregiver involvement"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 2 — Task Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Study activities such as:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Opening containers"},{"text":"Cutting"},{"text":"Pouring"},{"text":"Holding utensils"},{"text":"Turning knobs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 3 — Identify Problems"},{"type":"h","text":"Map:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Task","Difficulty","Cause","Design Opportunity"]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 4 — Prototype"},{"type":"p","text":"Develop adaptive tools."},{"type":"h","text":"Step 5 — User Testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Evaluate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Grip"},{"text":"Force"},{"text":"Comfort"},{"text":"Ease of use"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Independence"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Step 6 — Iterate"},{"type":"p","text":"Modify the design using user feedback."},{"type":"h","text":"Final portfolio story"},{"type":"flow","items":["User Need","Research","Task Analysis","Concept","Prototype","Testing","Iteration","Final Product"]}]},{"heading":"Certifications & Learning","kind":"certifications","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Useful areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Human-centred design"},{"text":"Universal design"},{"text":"Inclusive design"},{"text":"Accessibility"},{"text":"Human factors"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Healthcare design"},{"text":"Medical product design"},{"text":"Rehabilitation technology"},{"text":"CAD"},{"text":"3D printing"},{"text":"Product development"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Useful software:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Fusion 360"},{"text":"SolidWorks"},{"text":"Rhino"},{"text":"Blender"},{"text":"KeyShot"},{"text":"Adobe Illustrator"},{"text":"Photoshop"},{"text":"Figma"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, real user research and functional prototypes are generally more valuable than collecting generic design certificates."}]},{"heading":"Careers You Can Be Hired As","kind":"careers","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Possible entry-level roles:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Junior Assistive Product Designer"},{"text":"Assistive Technology Designer"},{"text":"Healthcare Product Designer"},{"text":"Medical Product Designer"},{"text":"Industrial Designer"},{"text":"Human Factors Design Assistant"},{"text":"Accessibility Designer"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Product Designer"},{"text":"Product Development Designer"},{"text":"UX Researcher"},{"text":"Inclusive Design Researcher"}]},{"type":"h","text":"With experience:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Senior Assistive Product Designer"},{"text":"Human Factors Specialist"},{"text":"Inclusive Design Specialist"},{"text":"Accessibility Design Lead"},{"text":"Healthcare Innovation Designer"},{"text":"Assistive Technology Lead"},{"text":"Design Research Lead"}]},{"type":"note","label":"Note","text":"Designing a medical device is different from practising as a regulated healthcare professional. Product designers work with clinicians, engineers, therapists and regulatory specialists where appropriate."}]},{"heading":"Interview Preparation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Technical Questions"},{"type":"h","text":"Prepare for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"What is universal design?"},{"text":"What is inclusive design?"},{"text":"Difference between accessibility and usability"},{"text":"What is anthropometry?"},{"text":"How do you design for limited dexterity?"},{"text":"How would you test an assistive product?"},{"text":"How do you balance independence and safety?"},{"text":"How do you select materials for a healthcare product?"},{"text":"How do you involve users in the design process?"},{"text":"How do you design for multiple physical abilities?"},{"text":"What is human factors engineering?"},{"text":"How would you identify usability risks?"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Design Challenge"},{"type":"h","text":"Example:"},{"type":"h","text":"\"Design a product that helps an older adult safely open medicine bottles.\""},{"type":"h","text":"A strong process:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Observe","Understand limitations","Define task","Identify risks","Prototype","Test","Iterate"]}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Structure","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"An assistive-design portfolio should prioritise evidence of impact."},{"type":"h","text":"Project 1 — Adaptive Everyday Product"},{"type":"h","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User problem"},{"text":"Research"},{"text":"Accessibility considerations"},{"text":"Prototype"},{"text":"Testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 2 — Mobility Product"},{"type":"h","text":"Demonstrate:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Safety"},{"text":"Physical interaction"},{"text":"Product architecture"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 3 — Sensory Accessibility"},{"type":"h","text":"Create a product addressing:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Visual"},{"text":"Auditory"},{"text":"Tactile"},{"text":"Or multimodal accessibility"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 4 — Rehabilitation Product"},{"type":"h","text":"Show:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User journey"},{"text":"Task analysis"},{"text":"Functional requirements"},{"text":"Prototype"},{"text":"Testing"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Project 5 — Smart Assistive Product"},{"type":"h","text":"Combine:"},{"type":"flow","items":["Physical Product","Sensors","Digital Interface"],"sep":"+"}]},{"heading":"High-Value Specialist Routes","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Route A — Assistive Technology"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Assistive Design Internship","Product Designer","Assistive Technology Specialist","Design Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Focus on technology-enabled independence."},{"type":"h","text":"Route B — Human Factors"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Human Factors Internship","Usability Research","Human Factors Specialist","Senior Specialist"]},{"type":"p","text":"Strong option for healthcare and medical-product industries."},{"type":"h","text":"Route C — Rehabilitation Products"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Rehabilitation Design","Product Development","Rehabilitation Product Specialist"]},{"type":"h","text":"Work closely with:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Physiotherapists"},{"text":"Occupational therapists"},{"text":"Rehabilitation professionals"},{"text":"Engineers"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Route D — Inclusive Consumer Products"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Inclusive Design","Consumer Products","Accessibility Design Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Apply accessibility principles beyond healthcare."},{"type":"h","text":"Route E — Social-Impact Design"},{"type":"flow","items":["B.Des","Community Design","Assistive Product Development","Social Innovation Lead"]},{"type":"p","text":"Particularly relevant for affordable and locally manufacturable solutions."}]},{"heading":"Assistive Product Design Workflow","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"A professional project can follow:"},{"type":"h","text":"User / Community Research"},{"type":"h","text":"Context Observation"},{"type":"h","text":"Task Analysis"},{"type":"h","text":"Functional Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Accessibility Requirements"},{"type":"h","text":"Concept Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Prototype"},{"type":"h","text":"User Testing"},{"type":"h","text":"Risk & Safety Review"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Iteration"},{"type":"h","text":"Engineering Development"},{"type":"h","text":"Validation"},{"type":"h","text":"Manufacturing"},{"type":"p","text":"This workflow ensures that the product is designed around actual user capability rather than assumptions."}]},{"heading":"Portfolio Projects to Build Before Graduation","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"table","header":["Project","Main Skill"],"rows":[[{"text":"Adaptive Kitchen Tool"},{"text":"Dexterity"}],[{"text":"Senior-Friendly Bathroom Product"},{"text":"Safety"}],[{"text":"Wheelchair Accessory"},{"text":"Mobility"}],[{"text":"Adaptive Writing Tool"},{"text":"Fine motor control"}],[{"text":"Accessible Medication Organiser"},{"text":"Cognitive + physical accessibility"}],[{"text":"Rehabilitation Device"},{"text":"Human factors"}],[{"text":"Low-Vision Household Product"},{"text":"Sensory accessibility"}],[{"text":"Adaptive Sports Equipment"},{"text":"Inclusive performance"}],[{"text":"Smart Assistive Device"},{"text":"Technology"}],[{"text":"Affordable Community Assistive Product"},{"text":"Social-impact design"}]]}]},{"heading":"AI and Future of Assistive Design","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI will increasingly enable:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Personalised assistive devices"},{"text":"Computer-vision assistance"},{"text":"Voice-controlled products"},{"text":"Predictive rehabilitation"},{"text":"Adaptive interfaces"},{"text":"Smart mobility systems"},{"text":"Gesture recognition"},{"text":"Personalised prosthetic/orthotic interfaces"},{"text":"AI-powered communication tools"},{"text":"Context-aware assistive environments"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For example, an assistive device could potentially adapt its behaviour based on:"},{"type":"flow","items":["User","Context","Behaviour","AI interpretation","Assistance"]},{"type":"p","text":"However, AI-based assistive products require particularly careful attention to safety, reliability, accessibility, privacy and human oversight."}]},{"heading":"Emerging Design Opportunities","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"AI Accessibility"},{"type":"p","text":"Design products that help users interact with technology through:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Voice"},{"text":"Vision"},{"text":"Gesture"},{"text":"Natural-language interaction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Smart Mobility"},{"type":"h","text":"Explore:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Connected mobility aids"},{"text":"Navigation assistance"},{"text":"Obstacle detection"},{"text":"Smart wheelchairs"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Age-Friendly Design"},{"type":"h","text":"Develop products supporting:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Independent living"},{"text":"Home safety"},{"text":"Medication management"},{"text":"Daily activities"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Affordable Assistive Technology"},{"type":"h","text":"Focus on:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Local manufacturing"},{"text":"Open-source designs"},{"text":"Low-cost materials"},{"text":"Repairability"},{"text":"Modular construction"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Adaptive Products"},{"type":"p","text":"Products that physically change according to:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"User ability"},{"text":"Body dimensions"},{"text":"Activity"},{"text":"Environment"}]}]},{"heading":"Study Abroad Options","kind":"abroad","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Relevant postgraduate areas include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Industrial Design"},{"text":"Inclusive Design"},{"text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"text":"Healthcare Design"},{"text":"Medical Product Design"},{"text":"Human Factors"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Engineering"},{"text":"Assistive Technology"},{"text":"Interaction Design"},{"text":"Design Research"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Potential destinations include:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"UK"},{"text":"USA"},{"text":"Canada"},{"text":"Germany"},{"text":"Netherlands"},{"text":"Sweden"},{"text":"Denmark"},{"text":"Australia"},{"text":"Japan"}]},{"type":"p","text":"For this career, look for programs with accessibility labs, human-factors research, healthcare partnerships, prototyping facilities and real-user testing opportunities."}]},{"heading":"Postgraduate Pathways","kind":"pg_india","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Design"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"M.Des Industrial Design"},{"text":"M.Des Product Design"},{"text":"MA Inclusive Design"},{"text":"MA Healthcare Design"},{"text":"MFA Industrial Design"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Human Factors"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Human Factors"},{"text":"MSc Human-Computer Interaction"},{"text":"Ergonomics"},{"text":"Usability Engineering"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Healthcare Technology"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"MSc Medical Product Design"},{"text":"Assistive Technology"},{"text":"Rehabilitation Technology"},{"text":"Healthcare Innovation"}]},{"type":"h","text":"Advanced Research"},{"type":"h","text":"A PhD can be useful for:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"Assistive technology research"},{"text":"Human factors research"},{"text":"Rehabilitation design"},{"text":"Accessibility research"},{"text":"Healthcare innovation"}]}]},{"heading":"Career Progression","kind":"growth","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"0–2 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Junior Assistive Product Designer / Design Researcher"},{"type":"h","text":"2–5 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Assistive Product Designer / Healthcare Product Designer"},{"type":"h","text":"5–8 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Senior Designer / Human Factors Specialist"},{"type":"h","text":"8–12 Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Lead / Assistive Technology Lead"},{"type":"h","text":"12+ Years"},{"type":"h","text":"Design Director / Head of Innovation / Assistive Technology Strategy Lead"}]},{"heading":"2040–2046 Career Evolution","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"p","text":"Assistive Product Design is likely to expand toward:"},{"type":"list","items":[{"text":"AI-powered accessibility"},{"text":"Human-AI assistive systems"},{"text":"Smart prosthetics"},{"text":"Adaptive robotics"},{"text":"Wearable assistive technology"},{"text":"Brain-computer interface products"},{"text":"Intelligent mobility systems"},{"text":"Personalised rehabilitation"},{"text":"Smart-home accessibility"},{"text":"AI-powered communication devices"}]},{"type":"p","text":"The designer may increasingly become an architect of human capability and independence, combining physical products with digital and intelligent systems."}]},{"heading":"Recommended Final Skill Stack","kind":"other","blocks":[{"type":"h","text":"Human-Centred Design"},{"type":